      },
      "message": "fix(post): refuse a canned cycle with no feed and a Tormach cut with the spindle stopped\n\nA canned cycle whose FeedRate is missing or not positive is refused by\nname in every post that writes the cycle's own F (tormach, fanuc, haas,\nsinumerik, mazak, doosan-dnm, grblhal, fanuc-lathe); heidenhain no\nlonger falls back to the last modal feed. tormach.cps also refuses a\nfeed, arc or cycle with the spindle stopped (no S.. M3 since the last\nM5), a touch probe's 0 rpm section exempt.\n\nThe Tormach mill goldens are now runnable 770MX programs, posted from\nthe legacy streams dressed with setup/operation/tool records, a tool\nchange, a spindle speed and each cycle's chain feed\n(tests/common/legacy_program.rs); every other dialect's drill and tap\ngoldens gain the cycle's F. The other spindle mill posts take the\nspindle rule in #1359.\n\nFixes #1357\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
