      "message": "fix(post): a Tormach probe exemption needs a touch-probe tool; pin the modal-feed fallback\n\nReview of PR #1367 (M3, safety tier):\n\n- tormach.cps exempted every section stating SpindleSpeed 0 from the\n  spindle-stopped refusal as a touch probe, so a cutting tool at 0 rpm\n  posted M5 and then G1 F.. with no refusal. The exemption now needs a\n  stated 0 rpm AND PARAM ToolKind \"touch probe\" (what posting.rs writes\n  for ToolKind::Probe); a cutter at 0 rpm, or a 0-rpm section stating no\n  tool kind, is refused by name.\n- The no-feed pins could not see Heidenhain falling back to the last\n  modal feed (their streams had no earlier F). A new case feeds first,\n  then drills a hole whose cycle and chain state no feed, through\n  heidenhain and fanuc: both must refuse by name.\n\nPins: a_tormach_cutter_section_stating_zero_rpm_is_refused_by_name,\na_tormach_touch_probe_section_still_posts,\na_cycle_with_no_feed_after_an_earlier_f_is_refused_by_name.\nprobe_spindle_stop's probe Dump now states its touch-probe kind.\n\nRefs #1357\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
