      "message": "fix(post): refuse a cut with the spindle stopped in every spindle mill dialect\n\nThe spindle-state rule #1357 gave tormach.cps (with the #1367 review's\ntouch-probe fix) is ported to fanuc, haas, sinumerik, mazak, heidenhain,\ndoosan-dnm, grblhal, tinyg and carvera. Each tracks the spindle from its\npreamble start (S.. M3; MOTON S..; M3 S..) to the next stop, and refuses\na feed, arc or canned cycle with it stopped, by name, posting nothing\nfor it. A touch-probe section (0 rpm on a PARAM ToolKind touch probe) is\nexempt; a cutter at 0 rpm is not. Heidenhain checks its native cycle\nafter the tapping refusals, so those keep their own names.\n\nEvery mill dialect's conformance golden is now posted from as_program\n(tool change, spindle speed, op comments), and the moved goldens are\nregenerated: lines are only added (setup/operation/tool comments, the\ntool change, the spindle start; Heidenhain and Sinumerik renumber).\nHeidenhain's tap_plate, refused before only for want of a spindle\nspeed, now posts and has a golden. Fixture streams in the post crate's\ntests and in fourth_axis_pose / tinyg_post state a spindle speed.\n\nPinned by post_spindle_rule_all.rs (feed, arc, hole, 0-rpm cutter vs\ntouch probe, section after the stop, per dialect).\n\nFixes #1359\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
